## Claim
Text: "India's Congress party candidate Maskoor Usmani installed Jinnah's portrait at AMU."
Claim author: Pooja Chaudhuri
Claim date: October 17, 2020
Claim origin: https://t.co/sf132cXZN6pic.twitter.com/Um6lIYhCI7

## Initial Q&A
### Was Maskoor Usmani a candidate for the Indian National Congress party in or around October 2020?
Answer: Yes, Maskoor Usmani was a candidate for the Indian National Congress party in October 2020. According to the search result, "The Congress Party has roped in former President of Aligarh Muslim University Student's Union Dr Maskoor Ahmad Usmani as a candidate from Jale seat, Dharbhanga for the upcoming Bihar Assembly Elections 2020 that is all set to start on October 28." The article notes, however, that "the party is yet to announce this officially," though he was included in Congress's list of candidates for the Bihar Assembly Elections.

Source URL: https://newsd.in/bihar-polls-2020-congress-fields-former-amu-students-union-president-maskoor-usmani-from-jale-seat/

### Is there photographic or video evidence showing Maskoor Usmani installing a portrait of Muhammad Ali Jinnah at Aligarh Muslim University?
Answer: Based on the search result, there is no photographic or video evidence presented showing Maskoor Usmani installing a portrait of Muhammad Ali Jinnah at Aligarh Muslim University. The source explicitly states that the claim is false, noting that "the portrait has been there since the pre-independence era" (since 1938) and that Usmani himself called the narrative "false propaganda."

Source URL: https://www.newsclick.in/aaj-tak-falsely-claims-congress-candidate-maskoor-usmani-hung-jinnah-portrait-AMU

### Did any official body or representative of Aligarh Muslim University issue a statement confirming or denying that a portrait of Muhammad Ali Jinnah was installed by Maskoor Usmani?
Answer: Yes, the Aligarh Muslim University administration issued statements denying that Maskoor Usmani installed the portrait. AMU spokesperson Shafey Kidwai explained that Jinnah's portrait has been in the students' union hall since 1938 because he was a founder and life member, and Vice-Chancellor Tariq Mansoor clarified to the Centre that "the portrait has been in the students’ hall since 1938 while Usmani had called it 'just a historical preservation of the university’s legacy.'"

Source URL: https://www.thequint.com/news/webqoof/aajtaks-claim-that-maskoor-usmani-hung-jinnah-portrait-at-amu-is-false

### What was the specific date and location within Aligarh Muslim University where the portrait of Muhammad Ali Jinnah was allegedly installed?
Answer: The portrait of Muhammad Ali Jinnah has been hanging in the Aligarh Muslim University (AMU) since 1938, specifically on the walls of the students' union hall, not installed in 2018 as claimed. According to an AMU spokesperson, "Jinnah was accorded life membership of the AMU students' union in 1938" and photographs of life members are traditionally placed there.

Source URL: https://www.thequint.com/news/webqoof/aajtaks-claim-that-maskoor-usmani-hung-jinnah-portrait-at-amu-is-false

### Was the installation of the portrait part of an official event, and if so, what was the event's purpose and who organized it?
Answer: The portrait of Muhammad Ali Jinnah was not installed as part of a specific official event; it has been displayed in the Aligarh Muslim University (AMU) students' union hall since 1938 as part of a longstanding tradition. According to the AMU spokesperson, "Jinnah was accorded life membership of the AMU students' union in 1938. Traditionally, photographs of all life members are placed on the walls of the student union." The claim that a recent candidate installed it is false.

Source URL: https://www.thequint.com/news/webqoof/aajtaks-claim-that-maskoor-usmani-hung-jinnah-portrait-at-amu-is-false

### Did Maskoor Usmani publicly acknowledge or claim responsibility for installing the portrait of Muhammad Ali Jinnah at Aligarh Muslim University?
Answer: Based on the search result, there is no evidence that Maskoor Usmani acknowledged or claimed responsibility for installing the portrait. In fact, he denied the allegations, writing to the Election Commission that such media claims were "blatant lies," and the AMU administration confirmed the portrait had been installed in 1938, long before Usmani's involvement.

Source URL: https://www.thequint.com/news/webqoof/aajtaks-claim-that-maskoor-usmani-hung-jinnah-portrait-at-amu-is-false

### Are there any contemporaneous news reports from October 2020 from credible Indian media outlets that describe this specific incident?
Answer: Yes, a contemporaneous October 2020 report from the credible Indian outlet **The Quint** directly addressed and investigated this claim. The article states that while news channel AajTak made the accusation, its own investigation found the claim to be false, noting: "there is no report to corroborate AajTak’s claim of Usmani having installed the portrait at the university." It further explains that the portrait had been on display since 1938 and that Usmani called the allegation "blatant lies."

Source URL: https://www.thequint.com/news/webqoof/aajtaks-claim-that-maskoor-usmani-hung-jinnah-portrait-at-amu-is-false

### Was the portrait of Muhammad Ali Jinnah already present at Aligarh Muslim University before October 2020, and was the action merely its reinstallation or unveiling?
Answer: Yes, the portrait of Muhammad Ali Jinnah was already present at Aligarh Muslim University long before October 2020. According to historian Irfan Habib, "the portrait came up in 1938" when Jinnah was given a lifetime membership by the students' union, and it had been hanging in the students’ union hall among other portraits ever since, with no significant controversy until recent years. Therefore, any action in 2020 was not its initial installation but a re-hanging or re-unveiling within an ongoing political dispute.

Source URL: https://frontline.thehindu.com/the-nation/jaundiced-perspective/article10108356.ece

### What was the stated reason or justification given by Maskoor Usmani or his supporters for installing the portrait of Muhammad Ali Jinnah?
Answer: According to the search result, the stated justification for the portrait's presence was not given by Maskoor Usmani for installing it, as the claim that he installed it is false. Instead, the AMU administration explained that the portrait has been there since 1938 because Muhammad Ali Jinnah was a founder of the university and was granted a life membership of the student union, with his portrait displayed as part of a tradition for all life members. Usmani himself described it as "just a historical preservation of the university’s legacy."

