## Final Judgement
Based on the recorded evidence, the key findings are that while Maskoor Usmani was indeed a Congress party candidate in October 2020, multiple credible sources—including statements from the Aligarh Muslim University (AMU) administration and fact-checking investigations—confirm that the portrait of Muhammad Ali Jinnah has been displayed in the AMU students' union hall since 1938. Usmani himself denied installing it, and there is no evidence to support the claim that he was responsible for its installation.

The evidence is clear and consistent, leaving no substantial gaps that require further investigation.

The claim that Maskoor Usmani installed Jinnah's portrait at AMU is explicitly and directly refuted by the available evidence, which shows the portrait's presence long predates his involvement and that he did not install it. Therefore, the decision is `refuted`.

### Verdict: REFUTED

### Justification
The fact-check finds the claim to be refuted. While Maskoor Usmani was a Congress candidate in October 2020, statements from the Aligarh Muslim University (AMU) administration confirm that the portrait of Muhammad Ali Jinnah has been displayed in the AMU students' union hall since 1938, as he was granted a life membership ([The Quint](https://www.thequint.com/news/webqoof/aajtaks-claim-that-maskoor-usmani-hung-jinnah-portrait-at-amu-is-false)). There is no evidence he installed it, and Usmani himself denied the allegations, calling them "blatant lies" ([Newsclick](https://www.newsclick.in/aaj-tak-falsely-claims-congress-candidate-maskoor-usmani-hung-jinnah-portrait-AMU)). The narrative was characterized as false propaganda.